  name "the-spellings-a-text-reads-are-pinned-by-bytes"
  note "A text case is read by the same reader on both sides, so a reader that took a spelling for the wrong value would agree with itself. Every value a text case reads appears in some bytes case, and this one holds the spellings the others do not: the two forms of a fraction, the escapes, bytes, a key that has to be quoted, an empty record and a named one."
